{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And Israel abode in Shittim.</b> This is what is written (Numbers 33:49): ״ויחנו על הירדן מבית הישימות עד אבל השטים״ — and they encamped by the Jordan from Beth-haYeshimoth as far as Abel-haShittim. Now were they not in the plains of Moab, for they had not moved from there, and from there Joshua sent spies?" "<b>By way of the Midrash.</b> וישב ישראל בשטים — there was a spring in Shittim that bred adulterers, for there are springs that breed the mighty and the weak, the beautiful and the ugly, the modest and those steeped in lewdness, and the spring of Shittim was one of harlotry; and it watered Sodom, and therefore it is written (Genesis 19:5): ״איה האנשים אשר באו אליך הלילה״ and so forth. And since that spring was cursed, the Holy One, blessed be He, is destined to dry it up and renew it, as Joel prophesied (Joel 4:18): ״ביום ההוא יטפו ההרים עסיס והגבעות תלכנה חלב וכל אפיקי יהודה ילכו מים ומעין מבית ה' יצא והשקה את נחל השטים״." "<b>And the people profaned themselves.</b> He made his holiness profane, in the manner of (Genesis 9:20): ״ויחל נח״ — for one who is fenced off from forbidden relations is called holy, and one who whores is its opposite. And every place where ״the people״ (העם) is said is an expression of disgrace: (Numbers 11:1) ״ויהי העם כמתאוננים״, (ibid. 20) ״וירב העם״, (ibid. 21) ״וידבר העם באלהים״, (ibid. 14) ״עד אנה ינאצוני העם״. And every place where ״my people״ (עמי) is said is an expression of praise: (Psalms 81) ״לו עמי שומע לי״, (Exodus 7:4) ״והוצאתי את צבאותי את עמי״, (Isaiah 40:1) ״נחמו נחמו עמי״. Thus they expounded in the Tanḥuma." "<b>To commit harlotry with the daughters of Moab.</b> Our Rabbis of blessed memory expounded — this is what people say: toss a stick into the air, it lands root-down. Who began with harlotry first? Lot, the father of Moab, as it is said (Leviticus 19): ״ותאמר הבכירה אל הצעירה״, and she called his name Moab — that is, from father (מאב). And the daughters took up their mother's spindle and would adorn themselves and go out perfumed before Israel and entice them with words, and eat and drink with them."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:36:04.303615896Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}